"""Single source for bundled offline policies, public Markdown and the source license."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
DOCS = {}
def document(key, title, sections):
    DOCS[key] = {'title': title, 'effective': 'Version 1.1 · Effective November 10, 2026', 'sections': [{'heading': h, 'body': b.strip()} for h, b in sections]}

document('privacy', 'Privacy Policy · Zero Telemetry', [
('In plain words', '''Still sends no analytics, usage events, advertising identifiers, automatic crash reports or viewing history to its developer. There is no Still account or developer-operated backend. Your settings stay on this device; your queue and pairing session stay in memory. This is what “zero developer telemetry” means in this app.

Playing online video necessarily contacts the chosen media provider. YouTube, Google, a stream host, your operating system and your network may process information under their own policies. This policy does not claim that online playback is anonymous or that no network traffic exists.'''),
('1. Who is responsible and what this covers', '''Still is developed by muneebwanee, reachable at https://github.com/muneebwanee. This policy covers the Still iPhone/iPad app, its bundled local browser remote and app-controlled data processing. It applies to this version from the effective date above. It does not govern GitHub, Apple, YouTube, browsers, routers or independently operated video sources.

The developer does not receive your playback activity through an app server. If you voluntarily contact the developer or publicly post an issue, the information you choose to provide is processed by the contact platform and may become public. Never include a pairing link or private media URL in a public report.'''),
('2. Information stored on your device', '''Still stores small preferences in iOS UserDefaults: onboarding completion, receiver name, appearance and color theme, compact-layout and haptic choices, screen-awake and auto-next preferences, skip interval, stream quality, repeat and speed preferences, queue-only mode and whether YouTube playback is allowed. These preferences are not a watch history and are not automatically sent to the developer.

During use, memory holds the current media URL and title, video ID where relevant, pending queue, playback position and duration, player volume and state, sleep-timer deadline, a local network address, the temporary pairing token and the time of the most recent accepted remote command. Queue and session information are not intentionally written to a persistent history database. User-provided titles and receiver names can themselves contain personal information, so avoid sensitive names when sharing a session.'''),
('3. Information Still does not collect for telemetry', '''Still has no analytics SDK, advertising SDK, tracking pixel, fingerprinting service, developer crash-reporting upload, telemetry endpoint or account identifier. It does not sell personal information, build advertising profiles, run advertisements of its own, or combine activity across applications for advertising. There is no developer-side viewing database to export or delete.

This promise concerns app-authored collection. Apple may receive diagnostics according to your device and App Store settings. Your browser or operating system may maintain independent logs, network records, backups or security reports. Still cannot change those settings or represent that such system records do not exist.'''),
('4. Local pairing and people on your network', '''Starting the receiver advertises Still’s own Bonjour service on Wi-Fi and opens a local HTTP listener. The displayed QR code contains a device address and a temporary random token. The token grants access to the local remote API until receiving stops. It changes on restart, on disconnecting all remotes, and after local wipe. No pairing information is sent to a developer server.

A paired remote can see the current title, source, playback status, timeline, player volume, queue titles and playback error. In full-control mode it can replace, queue, pause, resume, seek, stop or skip videos and change player volume. In queue-only mode it can read session status and add videos, while the receiver rejects transport and replacement commands. Queue-only is not a confidentiality boundary: paired users can still see titles and status.

Local remote traffic uses HTTP and is not encrypted. The token is an access credential, not encryption. A person intercepting your network traffic or obtaining the complete pairing link may control the receiver. Use trusted private Wi-Fi. Do not forward its listening port to the internet. Disconnect all remotes or stop the receiver when access should end.'''),
('5. Online media and YouTube', '''Direct-stream playback connects the receiving device to the URL you choose and possibly to hosts referenced by its media playlist. Such hosts may receive your IP address, request headers, media URL, access tokens included in the URL, timestamps, device or playback information and other network metadata. The browser remote sends the link to Still; Still does not proxy the video through its developer.

YouTube playback uses the official iframe API and privacy-enhanced embed host in a nonpersistent WKWebView data store. Loading the player and playing a video contacts YouTube/Google services, including their API and media hosts. They may receive your IP address, video identifier, device/browser information, playback events and other information under Google’s Privacy Policy at https://policies.google.com/privacy and YouTube’s terms at https://www.youtube.com/t/terms. Privacy-enhanced mode does not eliminate provider processing. Provider ads or cookies may be involved according to provider behavior and applicable rules.

You can disable YouTube playback in Privacy & Data. This stops a current YouTube video and removes queued YouTube entries; new YouTube loads are rejected while disabled. This control does not block network requests made by direct media sources, nor does it erase records already held by providers.'''),
('6. Permissions and device features', '''Still requests Local Network permission when you start receiving, for Bonjour advertisement and local commands. iOS decides whether and when to display the permission request. Denial can be changed in iOS Settings. The receiving iOS app does not request camera, microphone, photos, location, contacts, notifications or App Tracking Transparency authorization.

The receiving device displays a QR code; your other device scans it using its own camera or browser. Sharing a pairing link, document or support summary uses the system share sheet only after you choose to share. Still can keep the screen awake during an active session if you enable that preference. It releases that request when stopped or backgrounded. Optional haptics use supported device hardware without collecting interaction statistics.'''),
('7. Retention, caches and local wipe', '''Preferences remain until changed, wiped or removed with the app, subject to operating-system backup and restore behavior. The queue, timer and current session are memory-only app state. Stopping the receiver revokes its token and closes its connections; backgrounding also pauses playback. Stopping a video releases its current player item. Network and system media frameworks may buffer content or maintain caches as part of playback.

“Wipe local data now” first stops receiving and playback, then clears the queue, pairing, timer and app preferences, removes app-managed web data and URL caches, and attempts to delete the app’s cache-directory contents. The interface returns to onboarding. Cleanup may take a short time and displays progress. If file cleanup fails, the app reports that some cached files may remain rather than claiming full success.

Wipe is an app-level reset, not certified forensic erasure. It cannot delete data in another device’s browser, clipboard, screenshot, shared message, provider account, router, OS diagnostic record or existing backup. Another browser may retain previously displayed titles or form input. Stop sharing and clear that browser independently if needed. Uninstalling Still removes its normal app container under iOS rules; restoring a backup may restore older preferences.'''),
('8. Support, rights and safeguards', '''A support summary is generated only when you choose to share it. It contains the app version, OS version and generic receiver/playback status. It excludes your receiver name, Wi-Fi address, token, media URLs and titles. Review the system sharing destination yourself. No support report is automatically uploaded.

Depending on applicable law, you may have rights concerning information you voluntarily provide to the developer or a service provider. Contact the developer through the profile above for developer-held communications, and contact the relevant provider for provider-held playback data. Because Still has no account or telemetry database, it cannot identify or delete a server-side playback record that it never received. Provide only information necessary for your request.

Access tokens and input validation reduce accidental exposure but cannot guarantee perfect security. Report a suspected issue privately through available developer contact channels when possible. Avoid placing private credentials in public issues.'''),
('9. Children, international services and policy changes', '''Still is a general-purpose playback tool and does not knowingly collect children’s personal information for developer telemetry. A parent or guardian should supervise content access, network sharing and use of third-party services where appropriate. Follow provider age requirements and applicable local rules.

Choosing online media or an external support site may involve service providers operating in other countries. Still does not operate an international telemetry transfer service of its own. Policies of those providers govern their processing.

Future versions may change preferences or features. Material changes to this policy will be reflected in the bundled text and its effective/version information. This release contains no consent switch that secretly enables telemetry. Offline copies let you review the policy shipped with your installed version, even if the repository later changes.''')])

document('terms', 'Terms of Service', [
('In plain words', '''Use Still to watch video links you are entitled to use, on devices and networks you control or are authorized to use. Keep your pairing link private and expect the app to stay open while receiving. Still has no account or paid feature gate. It does not promise that every online video will play or that an iPhone becomes a certified Cast receiver.

These terms govern use of the app and local remote. The Store EULA governs the installed application license where distributed through a store. The Non-Commercial License governs the covered source and redistributions. Mandatory legal rights remain unaffected.'''),
('1. Agreement and developer', '''Still is provided by muneebwanee, whose developer profile and support contact is https://github.com/muneebwanee. By installing or using Still, you agree to these terms to the extent a binding agreement can be formed under applicable law. If you do not agree, stop using and uninstall it. If you use Still on behalf of an organization, you must have authority and a license that allows that organization’s intended use.

You must have legal capacity to enter the applicable agreement, or a parent or guardian’s appropriate permission. Follow the age and eligibility rules of YouTube and other services you choose to access. These terms do not themselves grant access to a third-party service or any particular video.'''),
('2. What the app provides', '''Still receives supported media links and playback commands from its bundled browser remote or compatible clients over a local Wi-Fi network. It offers on-device playback, a temporary queue, appearance preferences and session controls. Its own Bonjour advertisement identifies its own protocol. It is not a certified Google Cast, AirPlay or Miracast receiver and does not provide general-purpose screen mirroring.

The receiver must remain in the foreground. iOS can suspend networking, interrupt audio, restrict permissions or terminate the app. Backgrounding stops receiving and pauses playback in this version. The current implementation uses IPv4 Wi-Fi pairing. Supported extensions, codecs, formats and controls are described in the bundled compatibility page and may change as Apple or media providers change their platforms.'''),
('3. Your media and authorizations', '''You are responsible for choosing media, obtaining rights and following restrictions associated with it. Do not infringe copyright, unlawfully distribute another person’s private information, circumvent DRM or sign-in requirements, or bypass a provider’s embedding, geographic, age or access restrictions. Do not use Still to attack a network, harass another person, distribute malicious instructions or operate devices without authorization.

Still does not acquire ownership of your links or titles merely by holding them in memory for playback. Supplying a link authorizes the app to process it and request the associated media on the receiving device for your chosen session. This is not a license from the media owner to reproduce, publish or redistribute that media. A source-code license for Still grants no rights to YouTube videos, music, thumbnails, marks or other third-party content.'''),
('4. Local access and shared sessions', '''You decide when to start the receiver and who receives the pairing link. The link grants session access until revoked. A remote may see playback and queue information even in queue-only mode. Anyone you pair may submit unwanted links or choose disruptive actions within the selected access mode. Queue-only mode limits commands but does not verify that a submitted video is appropriate.

Use trusted Wi-Fi because remote traffic is local HTTP without transport encryption. Keep pairing credentials out of public posts and shared screenshots. Do not expose the receiver port to the public internet. Use Disconnect all remotes, Stop receiver or Local Wipe to revoke access. No setting guarantees protection against a person who can intercept or compromise your network or device.'''),
('5. Providers, availability and controls', '''YouTube playback uses the official embedded player and remains subject to YouTube’s terms, API rules, advertising, availability and restrictions. Some videos cannot be embedded, require sign-in, need an on-device tap or are unavailable in your region. Still does not extract YouTube media URLs, download YouTube videos, strip provider advertisements or bypass controls.

Direct streams depend on their host, valid TLS certificates, supported codecs and valid URL access tokens. Live media may lack a duration or seekable range. Stream quality settings request a ceiling where variants exist; they do not create variants or force YouTube quality. Speed, volume and repeat can depend on provider and media support. A command being accepted means it was handed to the player, not that the provider has guaranteed successful playback.

Internet access, network costs and hardware are your responsibility. The developer is not responsible for a third party removing a video or changing its service. Provider and device rules can affect features without any change to this app’s source.'''),
('6. Privacy and user-directed sharing', '''The bundled Privacy Policy explains zero developer telemetry, local preferences, temporary session state, provider requests and local wipe limits. Read it before sharing sensitive content. Still does not require a developer account or automatically upload viewing history or support diagnostics.

When you choose to share a pairing link, a support summary or a legal document, you select the destination in the system share sheet. Those destinations and any external links are independent services with their own rules. Do not include private media credentials in a public report. Local Wipe does not erase records held by those external services.'''),
('7. Application and source licenses', '''Your use of a store-installed app is subject to the bundled Store EULA and applicable platform usage rules. Source code and covered redistributions in this release are provided under Still Non-Commercial License (NCL) 1.0, a project-specific source-available license. That license allows specified non-commercial uses and is not an OSI-approved open-source license or a grant of unrestricted commercial rights.

Commercial source use, sale, monetized redistribution or commercial integration requires separate permission unless a stated exception or mandatory law applies. Earlier releases explicitly distributed under a different license retain the grants made for those copies. You must preserve applicable third-party notices and distinguish your modifications. No right to impersonate the developer, Apple, Google or YouTube is granted.'''),
('8. Charges, updates and changes', '''This version has no in-app purchase, subscription, premium unlock or developer advertising feature. This statement describes this version, not an undertaking that every future product will be distributed identically. Any store transaction is governed by its displayed terms and the platform’s applicable payment and refund rules. Your internet or mobile-data provider may charge for connectivity.

Updates may add, change or remove features for compatibility, reliability or legal reasons. You can review the bundled terms for the version you install. The app does not promise perpetual updates, a service-level agreement or lifetime compatibility with external platforms. No automatic background service should be assumed from the existence of a sleep timer or screen-awake option.'''),
('9. Warranty and limitations', '''To the extent permitted by applicable law, Still and its documentation are supplied as is and as available, without promises of uninterrupted or error-free operation, suitability for every purpose, availability of every source, or compatibility with all devices and networks. The developer does not warrant that every defect can be eliminated or that performance will always be smooth under every condition.

To the extent permitted by law, the developer is not liable for indirect, incidental, special or consequential losses, lost profits, lost content or loss of access arising from your use of Still or independent media services. This provision does not exclude liability that cannot lawfully be excluded, including applicable statutory consumer guarantees, mandatory remedies, or liability for conduct for which exclusion is prohibited. Any statutory right to repair, replacement, refund or damages takes precedence where applicable.'''),
('10. Ending use, disputes and contact', '''You can end use at any time by stopping the receiver and uninstalling the app. A material license breach may terminate applicable permissions under the relevant license’s terms, subject to any cure or statutory rights. Restrictions necessary to protect intellectual property and the warranty/liability provisions survive where legally enforceable.

These terms do not impose mandatory arbitration, a waiver of nonwaivable consumer remedies or a fabricated exclusive court venue. Applicable law and jurisdiction determine the parties’ available remedies. If a provision is unenforceable, the remaining provisions continue to the extent permitted by law. A failure to enforce a provision on one occasion is not a general waiver.

For support, accessibility concerns, permissions, commercial licensing or legal questions, contact muneebwanee through the developer profile above. A distributor offering this app under its own legal identity must supply accurate contact and legally required business details with that distribution. The repository’s release guidance identifies metadata that still requires the distributor’s review.''')])

