document('help', 'Connect in three steps', [
('1. Start on this screen', 'Connect your iPhone or iPad to Wi-Fi. Open Still and tap Start receiver. Allow Local Network access if iOS asks. Keep Still open.'),
('2. Scan from the other device', 'Put your other phone, tablet or computer on the same Wi-Fi. Scan Still’s QR code using that device’s camera. If scanning is difficult, use Share pairing link or expand Can’t scan the code? to copy the complete link.'),
('3. Send a video', 'In YouTube, choose Share → Copy link. Open the paired browser remote, paste the link and press Play now. Direct HTTPS media links work too. Add to queue keeps the current video playing. If queue-only mode is on, remotes can add videos while playback remains under this screen’s control.'),
('If it will not connect', 'Keep Still open and check that both devices use the same Wi-Fi. In iOS Settings → Privacy & Security → Local Network, allow Still. Guest networks, VPNs, captive portals, browser HTTPS-only settings and router isolation can block local pairing. Start again after a Wi-Fi change and scan the new code. Local pairing uses HTTP, so use trusted Wi-Fi.'),
('If a video will not play', 'Try another video to distinguish a bad source from a connection issue. YouTube videos may block embedding, require sign-in or need a tap on the receiver’s player. Use Open original when available. Streams need supported codecs, valid HTTPS certificates and an unexpired URL. Check that YouTube playback has not been turned off in Privacy & Data.'),
('Keep it simple', 'The everyday flow is Start → Scan → Play. Settings is optional. Try a sleep timer for bedtime or queue-only remotes when friends are choosing videos. Stop receiver ends remote access. Wipe local data resets the app when you want to start fresh.')])
document('compatibility', 'What works', [
('Devices and pairing', 'iPhone and iPad with iOS/iPadOS 17 or later. Local IPv4 Wi-Fi and modern sender browsers. The receiver stays open in the foreground. Bonjour announces Still’s own service; it does not create a YouTube Cast target.'),
('Video sources', 'YouTube watch, youtu.be, Shorts and live-video links that allow embedding. Direct HTTPS MP4, MOV, M4V, MP3, M4A and HLS (.m3u8) URLs with iOS-compatible codecs. Query-string access tokens are supported. Playlist pages, arbitrary web pages, custom authenticated headers and local HTTP media are not supported.'),
('Playback and session tools', 'Play/pause, seeking where supported, player volume, native stream full screen, queue of up to 20 items, queue editing, auto-next, repeat current video, supported playback speeds, skip intervals, HLS quality ceilings, session sleep timer and queue-only remotes. YouTube quality is managed by YouTube. Live media may lack a seekable timeline. iOS manages picture-in-picture availability through its native player where supported; Still provides no promise of background receiver service.'),
('Privacy and personalization', 'Five adaptive color themes, system/light/dark appearance, compact spacing, optional supported-device haptics, screen-awake setting, YouTube playback switch, zero developer telemetry, offline legal search, safe user-shared support summary and local wipe.'),
('Unavailable protocols', 'No certified Google Cast receiver, YouTube Cast-menu discovery, AirPlay receiving, Miracast, whole-screen mirroring, DRM bypass, YouTube downloading, internet-wide remote hosting or IPv6-only local pairing. No promise that all provider videos support embedding, speed, seeking or quality changes.')])
